### Real-time processing
Current Status: Partially Reached (~65%)
What is Reached:
In the browser, audio frames are analyzed continuously at ~60 FPS via requestAnimationFrame.
Sliding window averages and state transitions run every 1,000 ms.
Red-state SVG circular countdown updates every second in real time.
What is Missing:
The staff dashboard relies on HTTP polling every 1 second (setInterval(refreshDashboard, 1000)). While it looks real-time to the user, it puts unnecessary load on MySQL (60 database queries/minute per open browser tab) and has up to a 1,000 ms delay.
What Needs to Be Done:
Replace the 1-second setInterval polling with WebSockets (Socket.io) or Server-Sent Events (SSE).
When a room enters Red or an incident escalates, the server immediately pushes an event to all open dashboards in under 50 ms.
